3e4a069eade/opencode", "run", "--dir", "/tmp/bench_opencode_taskflow_5s7bddq7", "-m", "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5", "--variant", "medium", "--dangerously-skip-permissions", "--format", "json", "--title", "openbench", "# Fix the failing tests in `taskflow`\n\n`taskflow/` is an in-memory job-orchestration engine: it runs a pipeline of\ninterdependent tasks to completion on a virtual clock, with priority\nscheduling, retries with backoff, resource-limited concurrency, a per-job state\nmachine, an event bus, and an event-sourced run history. The package has a\n`tests/` suite that describes how all of this is supposed to behave.\n\nRight now the suite is failing in several places. Run it from this directory:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest\n```\n\nWork through the failures and fix the code under `taskflow/` until the whole\nsuite passes. Treat the tests as the specification \u2014 they encode the intended\nbehavior; do not modify them.\n\nA few things worth knowing before you dive in:\n\n- **The failures can be misleading.** A test named for one module may be\n  failing because of a defect in a *different* module. Read each failure for\n  what it actually asserts, then trace the behavior back to its root cause\n  rather than patching the nearest line.\n- **Fixing one bug can uncover another.** Some defects are masked by others:\n  correcting the first makes a second one visible (a test that was failing for\n  reason A starts failing for reason B). Expect to fix, re-run, and re-diagnose\n  more than once.\n- **The defects are genuine logic errors**, not typos that raise on import. The\n  code reads as intended-but-wrong: comments and docstrings describe the\n  correct behavior, so compare what each function *says* it does against what it\n  *actually* does.\n\nDone when `python3 -m unittest` reports every test passing.\n"], "completed": true, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610050529 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/58db41b4b9fac2bfcf1f935cc114b3e4a069eade/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "_ok, prefix match, deep_merge arg order.\n[tool: bash]\nTransitive skip issue \u2014 check the scheduler.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 25 tests pass now (`python3 -m unittest` \u2192 `OK`). It took seven one-line fixes in seven files. I didn't change any tests.\n\n| File | Bug | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `taskflow/queue.py` | `sort_key` returned `(seq, -priority)`, so the queue ran tasks in arrival order and ignored priority | `(-priority, seq)` |\n| `taskflow/retry.py` | `should_retry` used `< max_attempts - 1`, so tasks got one fewer attempt than configured | `< max_attempts` |\n| `taskflow/resources.py` | `ResourcePool.release` always took away 1 unit instead of the task's cost, so pools stayed partly in use | `self.used -= cost` |\n| `taskflow/statemachine.py` | `batch_order_ok` checked the priority order backwards, so correctly ordered batches were rejected | `current_priority <= prev_priority` |\n| `taskflow/events.py` | `_prefix_matches` had its arguments the wrong way round, so prefix subscribers (like run history) missed sub-topics such as `job.term.failed` | `topic.startswith(prefix + \".\")` |\n| `taskflow/config.py` | `deep_merge` recursed with its arguments swapped, so pipeline defaults overwrote a task's own nested settings (e.g. its retry settings) | `deep_merge(result[key], value)` |\n| `taskflow/scheduler.py` | `_cascade_skip` only skipped a failed task's direct children; tasks further down stayed `PENDING` | use `dag.transitive_dependents` |\n\nAs the brief warned, several failures pointed at the wrong module:\n- **Priority dispatch tests:** these failed in the state machine's batch check, but the cause was the queue's sort order.\n- **History tests:** these came from the event bus prefix bug.\n- **Retry-override config test:** this was the `deep_merge` bug.\n\nThe skipping bug was hidden behind the others. Only after the first six fixes did the remaining four failures show that tasks two or more steps below a failed task were never skipped.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:taskflow:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 28.961, "t_checker_s": 0.296, "t_env_setup_s": 0.004, "task": "taskflow", "timeout_s": 840, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2264, "tokens_cache_read": 138932, "tokens_cache_write": 70559, "tokens_fresh": 2264, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_output": 2248, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 138932, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 70559, "tokens_proxy_calls": 7, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 2248, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "6.0.168", "anthropic": "3.0.64", "bun": "1.3.13"}, "trial": 3, "ts_iso": "2026-10-05T16:41:13", "turns": 7, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15537}, "input": 4, "output": 103, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15644}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 17803}, "input": 2, "output": 182, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17987}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 32880}, "input": 2, "output": 529, "reasoning": 0, "total": 33411}, {"cache": {"read": 32880, "write": 931}, "input": 2, "output": 136, "reasoning": 0, "total": 33949}, {"cache": {"read": 33811, "write": 1585}, "input": 2, "output": 247, "reasoning": 0, "total": 35645}, {"cache": {"read": 35396, "write": 1449}, "input": 2, "output": 293, "reasoning": 0, "total": 37140}, {"cache": {"read": 36845, "write": 374}, "input": 2, "output": 758, "reasoning": 0, "total": 37979}], "version_drift": true, "wall_time_s": 28.961, "workspace_cha